tools.description:
Generate images or videos on Google Flow (flow.google.com) through the user's own browser session (free, no API). flow-text-to-image, flow-image-to-image — Nano Banana Pro/2/Lite; flow-text-to-video, flow-frame-to-video, flow-ingredients-to-video — Omni Flash / Veo 3.1 Lite|Fast|Quality, 4/6/8/10s, 16:9 or 9:16 only; flow-extend-video — lengthen the Veo clip the user currently has open in Flow's scene editor, prompt = what happens next. Returns the local file paths of the downloaded media if it finishes within ~40 s; otherwise returns a job id — keep calling flow_get_job with it until the job is done. Flow generation is deliberately slow and low-concurrency (anti-bot pacing) — a long wait or a 'cooldown active' status is expected behavior, not a bug.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__flow_connector__flow_generate(args: {
  aspect_ratio?: "16:9" | "9:16" | "1:1" | "2:3" | "3:2" | "4:3" | "3:4";
  // video duration in seconds
  duration?: "4" | "6" | "8" | "10";
  // download subfolder under Chrome Downloads
  folder?: string;
  // image: nano-banana-pro|nano-banana-2|nano-banana-2-lite — video: omni-flash|veo-3.1-lite|veo-3.1-fast|veo-3.1-quality (quality is the expensive one)
  image_model?: "nano-banana-pro" | "nano-banana-2" | "nano-banana-2-lite" | "omni-flash" | "veo-3.1-lite" | "veo-3.1-fast" | "veo-3.1-quality";
  // absolute local paths of input images (image-to-image / frame / ingredients)
  image_paths?: Array<string>;
  // generation mode
  mode: "flow-text-to-image" | "flow-image-to-image" | "flow-text-to-video" | "flow-frame-to-video" | "flow-ingredients-to-video" | "flow-video-to-video" | "flow-create-character" | "flow-set-voice" | "flow-extend-video" | "flow-rename-asset" | "flow-upload-assets";
  outputs?: number;
  // the generation prompt
  prompt: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Check the bridge: is the daemon up, is the extension connected, plan usage, active jobs, and whether an anti-bot cooldown is active.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__flow_connector__flow_status(args: {
  // which extension's status to check
  site?: "flow";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
